                        'Boot</strong>, a supported 64-bit processor, and enough RAM and storage (Windows 11 needs at least 4\xa0GB of RAM and 64\xa0GB of storage). Often TPM and Secure Boot are '
                        'simply switched off in the BIOS/UEFI and we can turn them on for you.</li><li><strong>A full backup before we touch anything</strong> — your documents, photos and email are '
                        'safely copied first, so nothing is ever at risk.</li><li><strong>The upgrade itself</strong> — either an in-place upgrade (keeping your apps, files and settings) or, where a '
                        'machine will benefit from a fresh start, a clean install with everything moved across afterwards.</li><li><strong>A tidy finish</strong> — drivers updated, security settings '
